    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09846v1</id>
    <title>Ensemble Methodology for Reference-Free Confidence Estimation in LLM-based Code Summarization</title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T18:29:48Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09846v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.09846v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>This paper describes an approach and use case to estimate the correctness of LLM-generated COBOL summaries without access to human-authored references. The core intuition is that inter-model agreement on semantics is informative about truth, and that an LLM-as-judge can provide higher-fidelity pairwise assessments than traditional string- or embedding-based metrics. We operationalise this intuition with (i) controlled summary generation from diverse models; (ii) a LLM evaluator that compares pairs of summaries and emits structured judgments; and (iii) a calibrated aggregation rule that combines supportive evidence while penalising only corroborated contradictions.</summary>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
