    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09342v1</id>
    <title>Syn2DRE: Synergistic Dual Teacher-Student Framework for Document-level Relation Extraction</title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T11:40:53Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.09342v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.09342v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Document-level Relation Extraction (DocRE) aims to identify relations between entities across a document but typically relies on costly large-scale annotations. While pseudo-labelling enables the use of low-quality data, existing methods often suffer from inefficiency and confirmation bias. To address these challenges, we propose Syn2DRE, a semi-supervised framework that combines self-supervised learning with cross-supervision in a lightweight teacher-student architecture to produce more reliable pseudo-labels. Additionally, we introduce a unified end-to-end training strategy to further improve efficiency of the framework. Experiments on multiple benchmarks show that Syn2DRE consistently outperforms prior state-of-the-art semi-supervised DocRE methods.</summary>
